A||||4||Shaun41178||How much? 260!! That's a shame.||||1
Z||000000||Shaun41178||09-28-1999||02:16 AM||||Went out Friday night to look for some trouble. My unbeaten streak on the street is still up for grabs and I was thinking that this could just be the night that it might happen. Opened my valve and off I went. Temp was around 55-65 degrees or so here in NW OH tonight and since I don't have a bottle warmer I knew that bottle pressure was down. I don't know how much it was down cause I don't have a gauge either. Yes call me stingy but I still don't feel I need either of them. If I ever want to keep my bottle warm I just place a few bottles of warm to hot water next to my bottle, make sure they don't slide anywhere, and then cover it all up with a bed blanket. Call me cheap people but it works. No warm bottles tonight though.<P>Anyway cruising up and down the same couple streets all night and nothing has come close to becoming a "rush". Many 3rd and 4th gen f-bods and Mustangs were going in the opposite directions and sometimes I wished I had turned around to get them but I never did. <P>So cruising along and traffic is lightening a bit as it is getting close to 12:30. About 2 cars ahead of me and about 3 cars behind me total when a late model (90's) red Ford Thunderbird came up along my side and sat there for a sec but couldn't really go anywhere as there was a car ahead of both of us and I looked over a few times at him but he never looked over at me so I didn't think he wanted to go. Plus he wasn't revving or anything like that so I kind of wasn't sure. But I thought to myself that if he wanted to go at it he would follow me through the two cars that were up ahead of us so I sped up and weaved between the two cars(using blinker had plenty of room) to see if he would follow. Sure enough he did and then lined up next to me so I goosed it a few times and each time he pulled right up even with my front bumper. So then I gave it a 2 second punch and then let off since I had the jump to let him catch up and then when he was even with me I punced it again. Man it was beautiful! We were neck and neck from about 45-55 and then up to about 70 I slowly pulled a half car on him before shutting down. We both slowed for a light up ahead and since he was left of me he quickly turned into a gas station so I followed thinking he might want to talk. He pulled a u-turn in the gas station and jumped back out on the same street we were on except he was now going in the opposite direction and while pulling out he left some nice rubber. I followed him of course but didn't burn any rubber.<BR>Now going in the opposite direction there are absolutely no cars up ahead for about a good mile but there was a crest in the road so I waited to get past that before proceeding to get next to him. Went over the crest so I got next to him and as soon as I got next to him he gunned it and when he did I did as well. He had a slight bumper on me from the jump at about 40 but I quickly made that up and then proceeded to pull a half car again to 70 as my tranny hadn't shifted to 3rd yet when I shut down again.<P>We appraoched traffic up ahead and slowed to about 25 as he pulled up next to me and asked what I had and I told him the V6. He said that the V6's were nice and then that my car was light so it gave me a slight advantage but he didn't say it in a way like he was making excuses. He asked if I had the 5 speed and i said "No I have the automatic". He turned to his colleague right of him and told him that I had the auto tranny in a sort of amazed voice. While we are talking a load of traffic is building up behind us cause we are doing 25-30 in a 45 mph zone. Kind of funny actually. So I ask him "What kind of engine you got and how much horsepower is your car rated at?" He said "Its the supercharged V6 and it's 260 hp." A couple of more words were exchanged before we decided to part ways and then he turned into a small parking lot. The guy was cool. I never did tell him I was running nitrous as he didn't ask. I can only assume he thought he got beat by a relatively stock Fiero. I did tell him that I have run a 14.2 and he says "I bet it does, its quick"<P>Didn't get anymore "contestants" for the rest of the night but almost came close to getting a vette but guy was going too fast for me to want to get up next to him plus he was weeving a bit so I think the person might have been partially or totally intoxicated. So I wanted no part of that. Still haven't had a vette next to me as I can't wait see what his/her face does when I slowly pull or hang right with them.<P>Arriving home I parked it and shut the valve on my bottle and told myself that perahps next week will be the week when I see taillights. As far as this week i thank that I made it through without being beat and that I was not the cause or involved in some sort of accident or a run in with the men in blue.<P>Whew!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||K9||09-28-1999||05:16 AM||||What type opf nitro are you running and what mods. have you done to your engine.I am thinking about nitro in my 85 GT. Do you recmond it or not?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||09-28-1999||05:20 AM||||So you have a supercharger on a 2.8 v6?  Or is it just nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||09-28-1999||11:15 PM||||As far as mods go I have nitrous oxide(70 shot), underdrive pulley, custom intake with K&N cone filter, ported exhaust manifolds, and rear sway bar.  You can see pics of my car and a few writeups on my mods on my webpage. <BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178</A> <P>I highly recommend nitrous oxide as I feel it has been the best thing for my car and gave the biggest increase in hp and torque for relatively little money.<P>I only have nitrous oxide.  I don't have a supercharger.  The car that I raced did have a supercharger however.<P>Shaun||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shiner||09-30-1999||10:18 PM||||Nice post!  This is the kind of stuff I love to see!<P>||||reg||7
